16. Model vs Compute Home

CNS must permanently distinguish these two concepts.

MODEL

The intelligence/model family:

Qwen
DeepSeek
GLM
Kimi
Mistral
Gemma
Future Model

COMPUTE HOME

Where that model is actually executed:

Local CNS server
Remote GPU
Cloud provider
Free inference provider
Paid API
Future compute home

Therefore:

> Model ≠ Compute Home.



A single logical model can have multiple compute homes.


---

17. Provider Failover

If remote models are eventually used, CNS should maintain a Compute Home Registry.

Example:

Model: Qwen

Home A
Status: healthy
Quota: available

Home B
Status: rate limited

Home C
Status: healthy

Local
Status: healthy

If Home A reaches its limit:

Home A ❌
     ↓
Home C ✅

The CNS brain's memory, identity and state do not move.

Only execution moves.


