19. Model-Agnostic Rule

This is a hard architectural rule:

> CNS must never be structurally dependent on Qwen, DeepSeek, or any other individual model.



Models are replaceable.

Model versions are replaceable.

Quantizations are replaceable.

Runtimes are replaceable.

Compute homes are replaceable.

The CNS core remains stable.


---

20. The "Best Available" Rule

When the user says:

> "Use the best available local model."



CNS should not blindly select a hard-coded model.

It should evaluate:

Available models
      ↓
Task requirements
      ↓
Capabilities
      ↓
Hardware
      ↓
Performance
      ↓
Latency
      ↓
Current health
      ↓
User policy
      ↓
Select model

This allows CNS to automatically adapt as better models become available.


---

21. The Three-Level Model Supply System

The long-term local model system becomes:

CNS LOCAL MODEL BUS
                         │
          ┌──────────────┼──────────────┐
          │              │              │
       SAME MODEL     SAME FAMILY    DIFFERENT FAMILY
       DIFFERENT      DIFFERENT      ALTERNATIVE
       HOME           VERSION
          │              │              │
          ▼              ▼              ▼
       Qwen A          Qwen 3.x       DeepSeek
       Qwen B          Qwen small     GLM
