---

24. Final CNS Principle

BUILD THE ROAD, NOT THE VEHICLE.

We are not building:

> "The Qwen system."



We are building:

> "The CNS Local Model Infrastructure."



Qwen can be one vehicle.

DeepSeek can be another.

GLM can be another.

A future model can become another.

A model can be replaced without rebuilding the road.

A quantization can be replaced without rebuilding the road.

A runtime can be replaced without rebuilding the road.

A compute server can be replaced without rebuilding the road.

And eventually, when you say in CNS chat:

> "Use whatever model is best for this job."



CNS should be able to make that decision itself according to the rules and available resources.

This is the architecture we should put into the CNS repository as the foundation for local LLM infrastructure.